1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
"…but your document says automatic replica failover is not configured."

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:12,000
"Recovery is manual. An on-call operator promotes a replica…"

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,500
YOU (interrupting): "Wait. I meant manual failover."

4
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:24,000
VIVA's voice stops. The claim is marked: cut off, awaiting your correction.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:32,000
The document is searched again. Contradicted → Supported.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
"That changes it. The document supports manual failover — section two, data storage."

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:55,000
This is VIVA RedTeam. Rehearse the questions your document cannot answer.

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Unsupported means the document is silent. "I can't find that in the supplied material."

9
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:45,000
The Voice Agent listens, takes turns, and speaks. The server holds the document and checks every claim. No tool can write a verdict.

10
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:05,000
The Defensibility Report: what held, what needed qualifying, what was contradicted, what is unsupported. No score.

11
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:30,000
For anyone who wrote something important and wants it attacked first. The claim check is lexical, and the README says so.
